---
title: Cocoa & Vanilla Oat Bites
author: graze
servings: 12
description: No-bake wholegrain oat flapjack bites flavoured with cocoa and vanilla, with mixed seeds - a homemade take on the classic cocoa & vanilla flapjack.
---

Line a #20cm square tin{} with baking paper.

Melt @golden syrup{100%g} and @butter{75%g} together in a #saucepan over low heat, stirring, until smooth and runny.

Take off the heat and stir in @light brown sugar{30%g} until dissolved.

Sift in @cocoa powder{20%g} and stir in @vanilla extract{1%tsp} until fully combined and smooth.

Add @rolled oats{220%g}, @linseeds{20%g} and @sunflower seeds{15%g} to the pan and mix well until everything is fully coated.

Stir in a pinch of @salt{1%pinch}.

Tip the mixture into the lined tin and press down firmly and evenly with the back of a spoon or spatula.

Chill in the fridge for at least ~chill{1%hour}, or until firm.

Turn out and cut into 12 bars or bites.

> Store in an airtight container in the fridge for up to a week.

> For extra protein, stir in a spoonful of soy or pea protein powder with the oats.
